menu "HID Example Configuration"
    config EXAMPLE_SSP_ENABLED
        bool "Secure Simple Pairing"
        depends on BT_CLASSIC_ENABLED
        default y
        help
            This enables the Secure Simple Pairing. If disable this option,
            Bluedroid will only support Legacy Pairing

    config EXAMPLE_LOCAL_DEVICE_NAME
        string "Local Device Name"
        default "HID Mouse Example"
        help
            Use this option to set local device name.

    config EXAMPLE_LIMITED_DISCOVERABLE
        bool "Advertise as limited discoverable (match RVL-CNT-01)"
        depends on BT_CLASSIC_ENABLED
        default y
        help
            A genuine Wii Remote in sync mode advertises Class of Device
            0x002504, which includes the limited-discoverable service bit, and
            answers the Limited Inquiry Access Code. Enable this to reproduce
            that behaviour. Disable it to fall back to general discoverable
            mode (CoD 0x000504) if the host performs a general inquiry
            instead. Verify the measured CoD with "hcitool inq --flush".

    config EXAMPLE_FAKE_BUTTON_DEMO
        bool "Cycle fake core buttons while connected"
        depends on BT_CLASSIC_ENABLED
        default n
        help
            Repeatedly press and release each of the 11 Wii Remote core
            buttons in sequence after the host selects continuous report 0x30.
            Keep disabled when using Wi-Fi web control.

    config EXAMPLE_WIFI_WEB_CONTROL
        bool "Enable Wi-Fi web button controller"
        depends on BT_CLASSIC_ENABLED
        default y
        help
            Connect as a Wi-Fi station and serve a local web page for Wii Remote
            button press/release control. Configure the station SSID and password
            below. Do not commit those credentials.

    config EXAMPLE_WIFI_SSID
        string "Wi-Fi SSID"
        depends on EXAMPLE_WIFI_WEB_CONTROL
        default ""
        help
            Wi-Fi station network name. Keep the password out of source control.

    config EXAMPLE_WIFI_PASSWORD
        string "Wi-Fi password"
        depends on EXAMPLE_WIFI_WEB_CONTROL
        default ""
        help
            Wi-Fi station password. This value is stored in the local ignored
            sdkconfig and compiled into firmware; never commit it.
endmenu
